  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "LESSON V"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "text": "CULTURAL NOTES"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "text": "HOTELS AND BOARDING HOUSES"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "text": "Italian hotels are called alberghi, although when a name follows, they may also be called hotel, as in Hotel Ambasciatori."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "text": "Motels are called motel and are usually found on highways."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "text": "Italian boarding houses are called pensioni."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "text": "A pensione is generally a family-run operation, usually smaller than a hotel though sometimes just as elegant."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "text": "In a pensione it is possible to have room and board."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "text": "Pensione completa includes the room, continental breakfast, and two meals; mezza pensione includes the room, continental breakfast, and one meal."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "text": "Not all rooms have private baths."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "text": "The casa albergo or \"residence\" is a relatively new institution that provides services similar to those of a hotel or boarding house."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "text": "It offers small, completely furnished apartments (1 to 3 bedrooms) with kitchen facilities."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "text": "They can be rented by the week or by the month."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "text": "Cleaning, house linen, telephone service, and utility services are provided by the management."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "text": "The case albergo are generally comfortable, conveniently located, and rather expensive."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "text": "In hotels, boarding houses, and the like, personal identification is requested at registration time."
    },
